What is deliberately not in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

An archived TypeScript snapshot of the upstream code was used, at an earlier stage,
as a read-only reference for parity comparison. It is not distributed here, was
never committed to this repository, and is git-ignored. See PARITY.md and
docs/LEGACY_SOURCE_BOUNDARY.md.

The Python material under `src/` and `tests/` is parity bookkeeping. It is not the
supported implementation, is not built, and is not covered by CI.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sego links against third-party crates from crates.io. Their licences are checked in
CI by `cargo deny check` against the allowlist and source policy in
`rust/deny.toml`; a crate whose licence is not on that allowlist fails the build
rather than being vendored silently.

This file records attribution for the source this project is derived from. It is
not a substitute for the dependency licence inventory that `cargo deny` maintains.
